        "file": "skills/playwright-test-generator/SKILL.md",
        "line": 51,
        "title": "Config discovery conflates config and source extensions",
        "evidence": "This line applies the same eight-extension set, including .jsx and .tsx, to Playwright config and spec discovery. The included playwright-debugger contract instead identifies six default config filenames at line 289, so environment detection can select a file the documented default runner would not discover.",
        "recommendation": "Define separate extension sets: the six documented default Playwright config extensions and the eight supported source/spec extensions; consider other config paths only when an approved command explicitly selects them."
      },
      {
        "severity": "M",
        "category": "security_trust_boundaries",
        "file": "skills/playwright-debugger/SKILL.md",
        "line": 438,
        "title": "Output template requests a raw artifact error",
        "evidence": "The finding template labels the Error field as a raw error message, conflicting with the same skill's untrusted-artifact boundary and its bundled reader's redact-before-output contract. Directly supplied or bypassed error text could therefore be echoed with credentials or hostile terminal content intact.",
        "recommendation": "Require a quoted, bounded, sanitized error excerpt and prohibit raw artifact-derived output regardless of how the error was supplied."
      },
      {
        "severity": "M",
        "category": "security_trust_boundaries",
        "file": "skills/cypress-debugger/SKILL.md",
        "line": 375,
        "title": "Untrusted title is used as a glob pattern",
        "evidence": "The guidance interpolates a report-derived test title into find -path. Shell quoting prevents command substitution but does not neutralize glob metacharacters in the title, so an attacker-controlled title can broaden or redirect artifact selection within the media root.",
        "recommendation": "Enumerate validated regular media files and correlate them through structured report metadata or exact component comparison; never treat a test title as a find glob."
      }
